# SRT.Core.Database.Postgresql (Cursor rule template)

This file is an **install template**. Copy it to the consumer project’s `.cursor/rules/` and keep the package-prefixed filename:

`SRT.Core.Database.Postgresql.CURSOR_RULE.mdc`

## Mandatory

Before using or modifying this package, follow:

- `docs/SRT.Core.Database.Postgresql.AI_RULES.md` (canonical)
- `docs/SRT.Core.Database.Postgresql.API_REFERENCE.md`
- `docs/SRT.Core.Database.Postgresql.COOKBOOK.md` for new DbContext / Repo / UoW

## Working rule

Read docs first. Do not invent APIs. If ambiguous, inspect related code and update the docs.

## Hard constraints (summary)

- Thin host `Program.cs`; no host `UseAuthorization` / `MapControllers`
- Shared scoped `PostgreSqlDataBase` across UoW repos; never dispose in repos
- `autoSave: true` saves entire context; `DeleteByFilterAsync` is immediate
- Bulk + tracked only inside `ExecuteInTransactionAsync`
- Whitelist order fields for user search input; `PaginationHelper.MaxPageSize = 500`
- `RunIdentityGapFix` default false; never `setval` downward at startup
- Cache / ErrorLog: inherit `PostgreSqlDataBase`, do **not** use Repo/UoW bases
- Durable cache is keyed `CacheServiceKeys.Sql` (`"sql"`); the key does not select SQL Server; `connectionType` does
- Postgres-only hosts: `connectionType` `postgresql` / `postgres` / `postgress`; do not reference SQL Server package
- Bind `Service` in every env appsettings
